WEBVTT

00:18.064 --> 00:18.364
Wee-yah!

00:36.882 --> 00:40.044
Leo brought us to the warehouse, left us in the

00:40.104 --> 00:45.066
cold Trying to buy a story, that was never being

00:45.086 --> 00:49.028
sold You looked at the archive, you looked at the

00:49.068 --> 00:53.830
frame You made a fatal error, and you didn't know

00:53.870 --> 00:57.372
the name You thought you bought a scandal, to put

00:57.512 --> 01:01.314
out on the wire But all you did was throw a heavy

01:01.414 --> 01:05.765
engine in the fire The angle of descent is

01:05.785 --> 01:09.549
cutting through the black! The shields are

01:09.569 --> 01:13.454
burning up and there is no turning back! The

01:13.474 --> 01:15.857
telemetry is screaming, the temperature is

01:15.917 --> 01:20.929
high! We're falling like a meteor across the

01:21.009 --> 01:24.972
open sky. Friction. Burning through the

01:25.153 --> 01:30.377
atmosphere. Friction. Everything is ending

01:30.457 --> 01:34.340
here. A heavy thermal blanket, a superheated

01:34.460 --> 01:38.383
glow. The absolute destruction of the only

01:38.423 --> 01:42.786
world you know. You wanted a reaction. You

01:42.826 --> 01:47.117
wanted the heat. I'm bringing down the fire to

01:47.137 --> 01:49.701
the middle of the street. Friction!

01:57.773 --> 02:00.656
I'm sitting in the chair while the television

02:00.696 --> 02:05.202
plays, waiting for the suit to cut through the

02:05.222 --> 02:09.406
haze. You walk into the room with a clipboard in

02:09.446 --> 02:13.691
your hand, making your demands like you own the

02:13.751 --> 02:19.153
heavy band. You cross out the lines, you tell us

02:19.233 --> 02:23.276
what to do But you don't have a clue what the

02:23.296 --> 02:26.518
metal's going through The angle of descent is

02:26.538 --> 02:30.300
cutting through the black The shields are

02:30.320 --> 02:34.203
burning up and there is no turning back The

02:34.223 --> 02:36.584
telemetry's screaming, the temperature is

02:36.644 --> 02:42.211
high We're falling like a meteor Across the open

02:42.251 --> 02:47.232
skies Friction Burning through the atmosphere

02:47.892 --> 02:52.214
Friction Everything is ending here A heavy

02:52.274 --> 02:56.375
thermal blanket A superheated glow The

02:56.455 --> 03:00.656
absolute destruction of the only world you know

03:01.076 --> 03:05.693
You wanted a reaction You wanted a heat I'm

03:05.733 --> 03:09.096
bringing down the fire to the middle of the

03:09.176 --> 03:10.357
streets. Friction!

03:45.878 --> 03:50.101
You looked at the camera, you called for shot 12,

03:50.421 --> 03:55.125
you pushed me to the edge of the broken shelf, you

03:55.205 --> 04:01.850
made your demand, and you crossed the final

04:01.870 --> 04:06.173
line!

04:06.353 --> 04:08.595
She's my sister!

04:26.544 --> 04:30.326
Friction, burning through the atmosphere

04:31.027 --> 04:35.309
Friction, everything is ending here A heavy

04:35.389 --> 04:39.472
thermal blanket, a superheated glow The

04:39.572 --> 04:43.754
absolute destruction of the only world you know

04:44.194 --> 04:48.797
You wanted a reaction, you wanted the heat I'm

04:48.857 --> 04:52.179
bringing down the fire to the middle of the

04:52.239 --> 04:53.440
street Friction

04:57.408 --> 05:01.115
Burn the contract, burn it in the atmosphere

05:01.175 --> 05:01.495
Friction

